# Line endings: every text file is stored with LF inside git, whatever core.autocrlf the machine has
# (a fresh clone in the cloud has no autocrlf=true). Blobs already in git are LF, so this rewrites none of them.
# Working-tree convention on the Windows machine + the commit gate: docs/HANDOFF.md §17 "CRLF" · .githooks/pre-commit
* text=auto
# Git hooks run under sh, which breaks on CR — they stay LF on every machine (the gate exempts eol=lf files).
.githooks/** text eol=lf
